-- 635: the Wild West tile is the old frontier (Kevin 2026-09-30: "wild west is all old frontier west, no modern settings ...
-- think the movie tombstone ... or red dead redemption era"). Every drawable spot on the 8 Wild West cards was checked
-- against the 1860s-1890s frontier and reviewed by hand. 52 deactivated: modern places (dams and reservoirs, ski and
-- resort areas, casinos, a motel, border walls, Mount Rushmore, Cadillac Ranch, a film studio's Western street, post-1900
-- towns), off-card ones (Pennsylvania's Strasburg / Lititz drift on Frontier Town, Patagonia, Uluru and Kings Canyon on
-- Cattle Ranch) and Ogden's 1924 station. 165 reworded: frontier places that carried a modern label
-- (National Park, State Historic Park, historic district, replica, Highway, Route 66): "Arches National Park Delicate Arch"
-- -> "Delicate Arch red sandstone span above canyon rim". Deactivated = is_active false (reversible). Re-runnable.

